TITLE:: Fosc User Guide
summary:: A SuperCollider API for generating musical notation in LilyPond.
categories:: Libraries>Music Notation
related:: Classes/Fosc, Classes/FoscMusicMaker, Classes/FoscScore, Classes/FoscStaff, Classes/FoscVoice, Classes/FoscNote

section::Description

link::https://github.com/n-armstrong/fosc##Fosc:: is a link::https://supercollider.github.io/##SuperCollider:: API for generating musical notation in link::http://lilypond.org/##LilyPond::.

strong::Fosc:: stands for FO-rmalised S-core C-ontrol (FO-r S-uperC-ollider).
It is a close relative of link::https://abjad.github.io/##Abjad:: and ports much of Abjad's Python code base to SuperCollider.

strong::Fosc:: lets you:

list::
##Create musical notation in an object-oriented way
##Generate and transform musical materials
##Construct powerful component selectors and iterators for modifying musical objects in a score
##Control all of the typographic details of music notation
##Play musical scores through scsynth
::

section::Installation

subsection::Install LilyPond

link::http://lilypond.org/##LilyPond:: is an open-source program that engraves music notation in an automated way.
strong::Fosc:: uses LilyPond to produce notational output.
It's recommended that you install the most recent version of LilyPond directly from the LilyPond website.

subsection::Install Fosc

Download the strong::Fosc:: master branch and unzip. Rename the 'fosc-master' folder to 'fosc'. Move the 'fosc' folder to your SuperCollider Extensions directory. Information on installing SuperCollider extensions can be found here: link::Guides/UsingExtensions::

subsection::Configure Fosc

In your sclang startup file, add code to allow strong::Fosc:: to communicate with LilyPond.

note::
It's possible that your LilyPond executable is installed somewhere different to the standard locations below.


list::

## macOS

code::
Fosc.lilypondPath = "/Applications/LilyPond.app/Contents/Resources/bin/lilypond";
::

## Linux

code::
Fosc.lilypondPath = "/usr/local/bin/lilypond";
::
::

Once you've saved your changes, recompile the SuperCollider class library and test that strong::Fosc:: is able to call LilyPond.

code::
Fosc.lilypondVersion;
::

Example output:

teletype::
2.19.82
::
::
SCDocHTMLRenderer
section::Creating score objects

subsection::Display a note

code::
(
a = FoscNote(60, 1/4);
a.show;
)
::
image::img/README-1.svg::

subsection::Display some notes in sequence

code::
(
a = FoscVoice([FoscNote(60, 1/4), FoscNote(62, 1/8)]);
a.show;
)
::
image::img/README-2.svg::

subsection::View LilyPond output in the Post window

code::
(
a = FoscVoice([FoscNote(60, 1/4), FoscNote(62, 1/8)]);
a.lilypond;
)
::

Example output:

code::
(
\new Voice {
    c'4
    d'8
}
)
::

subsection::Display a score

code::
(
a = FoscVoice([FoscNote("c'", 1/4), FoscNote("d'", 1/8)]);
b = FoscVoice([FoscNote("bf", 1/8), FoscNote("af", 1/4)]);
c = FoscScore([FoscStaff([a]), FoscStaff([b])]);
c.show;
)
::
image::img/README-3.svg::

section::Augmenting and tweaking score objects

subsection::Indicators attach to leaves

code::
(
a = FoscNote(60, 1/4);
a.attach(FoscArticulation('>'));
a.attach(FoscDynamic('f'));
a.show;
)
::
image::img/README-4.svg::

subsection::Spanners attach to two or more contiguous leaves

code::
(
a = FoscStaff(#[60,62,64,65].collect { |pitch| FoscNote(pitch, 1/8) });
a.selectLeaves.slur;
a.selectLeaves.hairpin('p < f');
a.show;
)
::
image::img/README-5.svg::

subsection::Override LilyPond grob properties

code::
(
a = FoscNote(60, 1/4);
override(a).noteHead.style = 'harmonic';
a.show;
)
::
image::img/README-6.svg::

subsection::Set LilyPond context properties

code::
(
a = FoscScore([FoscStaff(#[60,62,64,65].collect { |pitch| FoscNote(pitch, 1/8) })]);
set(a[0]).instrumentName = FoscMarkup("Violin");
set(a).proportionalNotationDuration = FoscSchemeMoment(#[1,64]);
a.show;
)
::
image::img/README-7.svg::

section::Creating music with FoscMusicMaker

subsection::Make music from durations and pitches

code::
(
a = FoscMusicMaker();
b = a.(durations: 1/4 ! 4, pitches: #[60,62,64,65]);
b.show;
)
::
image::img/README-8.svg::

subsection::Use a string of LilyPond note names

code::
(
a = FoscMusicMaker();
b = a.(durations: 1/4 ! 4, pitches: "c' d' ef' f'");
b.show;
)
::
image::img/README-9.svg::

subsection::Pitches are repeated cyclically when pitches is shorter than durations

code::
(
a = FoscMusicMaker();
b = a.(durations: [3/8,1/8,2/8,2/8], pitches: #[60,62]);
b.show;
)
::
image::img/README-10.svg::

subsection::Divisions embed into durations as rhythmic proportions

code::
(
a = FoscMusicMaker();
b = a.(durations: [2/16,3/16,5/16], divisions: #[[3,1],[3,2],[4,3]]);
b.show;
)
::
image::img/README-11.svg::

subsection::Negative divisions are rests

code::
(
a = FoscMusicMaker();
b = a.(durations: [2/16,3/16,5/16], divisions: #[[-3,1],[3,2],[4,-3]]);
b.show;
)
::
image::img/README-12.svg::

subsection::Rhythm cells repeat cyclically when durations is shorter than divisions

code::
(
a = FoscMusicMaker();
b = a.(durations: [1/4], divisions: #[1,1,1,1,1] ! 4);
b.show;
)
::
image::img/README-13.svg::

subsection::Rhythm cells repeat cyclically when divisions is shorter than durations

code::
(
a = FoscMusicMaker();
b = a.(durations: 1/4 ! 4, divisions: #[[-1,2,2],[4,-1]]);
b.show;
)
::
image::img/README-14.svg::

subsection::Apply a mask to fuse contiguous musical events

Mask patterns repeat cyclically. Pitches are added after the mask is applied.

code::
(
a = FoscMusicMaker();
b = a.(durations: 1/4 ! 4, divisions: #[[1,1,1,1,1]], mask: #[2,1], pitches: #[60,62]);
b.show;
)
::
image::img/README-15.svg::

subsection::Negative mask values are rests

code::
(
a = FoscMusicMaker();
b = a.(durations: 1/4 ! 4, divisions: #[[1,1,1,1,1]], mask: #[2,-1], pitches: #[60,62]);
b.show;
)
::
image::img/README-16.svg::

section::Selections

subsection::Select all score components

code::
(
a = FoscStaff([FoscRest(1/4), FoscNote(60, 1/4), FoscNote(62, 1/4)]);
b = a.selectComponents;
b.do { |each| each.cs.postln };
)
::

Example output:

teletype::
FoscStaff([  ], Staff, false, nil)
FoscRest(1/4)
FoscNote("c'", 1/4)
FoscNote("d'", 1/4)
::

subsection::Select notes and rests

code::
(
a = FoscStaff([FoscRest(1/4), FoscNote(60, 1/4), FoscNote(62, 1/4)]);
b = a.selectComponents(type: [FoscNote, FoscRest]);
b.do { |each| each.cs.postln };
)
::

Example output:

teletype::
FoscRest(1/4)
FoscNote("c'", 1/4)
FoscNote("d'", 1/4)
::

subsection::Select pitched leaves

code::
(
a = FoscStaff([FoscRest(1/4), FoscNote(60, 1/4), FoscChord(#[60,64,67], 1/4)]);
b = a.selectLeaves(pitched: true);
b.do { |each| each.cs.postln };
)
::

Example output:

teletype::
FoscNote("c'", 1/4)
FoscChord("c' e' g'", 1/4)
::

subsection::Attach indicators to all leaves in a selection

code::
(
a = FoscMusicMaker();
b = a.(durations: 1/8 ! 8, pitches: (60..67));
c = FoscStaff(b);
c.selectLeaves(pitched: true).do { |each| each.attach(FoscArticulation('>')) };
c.show;
)
::
image::img/README-17.svg::

section::Iteration

subsection::Iterate over all score components

code::
(
a = FoscMusicMaker();
b = a.(durations: 1/8 ! 8, pitches: (60..67));
c = FoscStaff(b);
c.doComponents({ |each| each.cs.postln });
)
::

Example output:

teletype::
FoscStaff([  ], Staff, false, nil)
FoscNote("c'", 1/8)
FoscNote("cs'", 1/8)
FoscNote("d'", 1/8)
FoscNote("ef'", 1/8)
FoscNote("e'", 1/8)
FoscNote("f'", 1/8)
FoscNote("fs'", 1/8)
FoscNote("g'", 1/8)
::

subsection::Iterate over notes, attaching indicators

code::
(
a = FoscMusicMaker();
b = a.(durations: 1/8 ! 4, mask: #[-1,1,1,1], pitches: #[60,61,62]);
c = FoscStaff(b);
c.doComponents({ |note| note.attach(FoscArticulation('>')) }, type: FoscNote);
c.show;
)
::
image::img/README-18.svg::

subsection::Iterate over runs, attaching slurs

code::
(
a = FoscMusicMaker();
b = a.(durations: 1/8 ! 8, mask: #[-1,1,1,1,-1,1,1,1], pitches: (60..65));
c = FoscStaff(b);
c.doRuns { |run| if (run.size > 1) { run.slur } };
c.show;
)
::
image::img/README-19.svg::

section::Playback

subsection::Playback using the default synth

code::
(
a = FoscChord([60,64,67], 1/4);
a.play;
)

a.show
::

code::
(
a = FoscStaff(FoscLeafMaker().((60..72), [1/8]));
a[0..].hairpin('pppp < ffff');
a.play
)

a.show
::

code::
(
a = FoscStaff(FoscLeafMaker().((60..63), [1/32]));
b = FoscStaff(FoscLeafMaker().((67..70), [1/32]));
c = FoscScore([a, b]);
c.play;
)

c.show
::

code::
(
a = FoscMusicMaker();
b = a.(durations: 1/4 ! 10, divisions: #[[1,1,1,1]], mask: [1,2,3], pitches: (60..63));
b.play;
)

b.show
::

subsection::Playback using pattern

code::
(
a = FoscStaff(FoscLeafMaker().((60..63), [1/32]));
p = a.pattern;
p.play;
)

a.show
::

code::
(
a = FoscMusicMaker();
b = a.(durations: 1/4 ! 10, divisions: #[[1,1,1,1]], mask: [1,2,3], pitches: (60..63));
p = b.pattern;
p.play;
)

a.show
::

code::
(
a = FoscStaff(FoscLeafMaker().((60..63), [1/32]));
b = FoscStaff(FoscLeafMaker().((67..70), [1/32]));
c = FoscScore([a, b]);
p = c.pattern;
p.play;
)
c.show
::

subsection:: Playback using custom synth

You can use your own synthdefs with Fosc's play mechanism by accessing the pattern property of any Fosc components or selection:

code::
s.boot;
(
SynthDef('beep', { |midinote, amp|
var src;
src = SinOsc.ar(midinote.midicps, 0, amp);
src = src * EnvGen.kr(Env.perc, doneAction: 2);
Out.ar(0, Pan2.ar(src, 0));
}).add;
)

(
a = FoscMusicMaker().(durations: [1/16], pitches: (60..72));
p = Pbindf(a.pattern, \instrument, 'beep');
p.play;
)

a.show
::

You can access the eventList property of any Fosc component or selection for making your own modifications or additions:

code::
a = FoscMusicMaker().(durations: [1/16], pitches: (60..72));
a.eventList;
::

subsection::Stop, pause and resume

subsubsection:: Stop

code::
(
a = FoscLeafMaker().(#[60,62,nil].wrapExtend(12), [3/8,1/8,5/16,1/16]);
a.play;
)

//a.isPlaying;
a.stop;
//a.isPlaying;

a.show
::

subsubsection:: Pause and resume

code::
(
a = FoscLeafMaker().(#[60,62,nil].wrapExtend(12), [3/8,1/8,5/16,1/16]);
a.play;
)

a.pause;

a.resume;

a.show
::


